    {
      "id": "2x8bjFQtm8n0bTr_tslRy",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1520.8333333333317,
      "y": 617255.8749999994,
      "width": 4339.311686197916,
      "height": 555,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bbI",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1718879012,
      "version": 141,
      "versionNonce": 480215588,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779017990568,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A vector space (or linear space) is a collection of vectors that is\nclosed under vector addition and scalar multiplication and satisfies eight axioms (e.g.,\nassociativity of addition, commutativity\nof addition, existence of an additive identity, etc.)",
      "fontSize": 111,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A vector space (or linear space) is a collection of vectors that is\nclosed under vector addition and scalar multiplication and satisfies eight axioms (e.g., associativity of addition, commutativity\nof addition, existence of an additive identity, etc.)",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "G52hfWmYsPWros8PGCuFF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1614.1666666666656,
      "y": 618010.6666666659,
      "width": 5081.871663411459,
      "height": 416.25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bbJ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 179057692,
      "version": 263,
      "versionNonce": 1814885276,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779018481579,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In machine learning, vector spaces are used to represent data points, features, and model parameters.\nFor example, in linear regression, the features of each data point can be represented as a vector in Rn,\nand the model parameters can be represented as a vector in the same space.",
      "fontSize": 111,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In machine learning, vector spaces are used to represent data points, features, and model parameters. For example, in linear regression, the features of each data point can be represented as a vector in Rn, and the model parameters can be represented as a vector in the same space.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
