      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Solving systems of equations: Many\nmachine learning algorithms, such as\nlinear regression, involve solving\nsystems\nof linear equations, which can be\neciently solved using\nmatrices. For example, the normal\nequation used to solve\nlinear regression is XT X✓ = XT y, where\nX is the design matrix, ✓ is the\nparameter vector, and y is the target\nvector.",
      "fontSize": 111,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Solving systems of equations: Many machine learning algorithms, such as linear regression, involve solving systems\nof linear equations, which can be eciently solved using\nmatrices. For example, the normal equation used to solve\nlinear regression is XT X✓ = XT y, where X is the design matrix, ✓ is the parameter vector, and y is the target\nvector.",
